# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Veil Bridge — the APP's environment.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Vite reads this at BUILD time and inlines the values, so anything here ships
# in the bundle and is public. Never put a private key or a secret in this file
# — the app never needs one. It signs with the user's wallet and nothing else.
#
# Every value has a working default except the two prover settings, so the app
# builds and runs with this file empty.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Which deployment file under ../deployments to load.
# `npm run demo` / `npm run build:demo` override this with demo.json.
VITE_DEPLOYMENT=ethereum-sepolia__starknet-sepolia.json

# Read-only RPCs, used for balances, quotes and the eligibility checks before a
# wallet connects. The Starknet one must serve RPC spec 0.8+: starknet.js v10
# cannot talk to an older node, and live Sepolia is on 0.10.x.
VITE_EVM_RPC_URL=https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com
VITE_STARKNET_RPC_URL=https://starknet-sepolia.drpc.org

# ── Creating an open note ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Needed for the "Create my open note" button, and ONLY for that. Everything
# else in the app works without them; unset, the button does not appear and the
# app says note creation is unavailable rather than failing inside the prover.
#
# Creating a note runs `create_open_note_derive` in the proven virtual block and
# submits `create_open_note_settle` with its proof. A browser can do neither, so
# the SNIP-36 prove-and-settle service does both.
#
# Deliberately no default: a hardcoded endpoint would send a holder's proof to a
# host nobody chose.
#
# These can also come from the deployment file, as `veil.proverEndpoint` and
# `veil.masterAddress` (set-addresses.js --prover / --master). This file wins.
VITE_VEIL_PROVER_ENDPOINT=

# The account the prover submits the settle FROM. Not a key: the browser cannot
# sign a settle, so the prover signs with its own account and this only names it.
VITE_VEIL_MASTER_ADDRESS=
